Yes, I had the same problem. There is a bitshift problem with the
float-to-int conversion in floatfns.c. Compiling with gcc will show the
warnings.
floatfns.c has a lot of changes compared to 19.22 but I closed my eyes
and replaced it with the 19.22 version and recompiled. 
Everything (including scrollbar) works fine now.

It's not a solution, I know. Just a quick hack.

