Huh ? Just because the X11 R5 libraries does not build with the current
public patches has very little to do with how applications build. 
R5 libX11 and libXt have been shipping from the first release of OSF/1
on Alpha. libX11 is designed to buffer the user from hardware and OS issues.
Yes libX11 required many changes (which have been incorporated into R6),
but this does not mean that vi 

90% of  the X related sources that I pull off the net build and operate 
without error AND without change. This includes Xv3.0:

To build Xv, 
	xmkmf
	cd jpeg; make libjpeg.a ; cd .. # makefile 'feature'
	make


There are a number of unique problems that a programmer/porter may encounter,
but almost all of these are related to use of bad practices (ie. the
Xt spec says don't do it that way), the use of properties format 32 
properties directly (which is rare), or int/long interchanging.


