mliggett@onyx.chem.indiana.edu (Matthew Liggett) writes:

>subject says it all.
>we have a 3000/600 with a small keyboard and can't figure out how to use
>the ESC key (which also houses ` and ~ if memory serves)

>thanks in advance.

You can use xmodmap to remap these keys.  It appears to be standard, if one
wants to make that the escape key, to remap ~ and ` to the key in the lower
left corner that has > and < on it.  The following lines in ~/.xmodmaprc should
do that for you

	keysym comma = comma less
	keysym period = period greater
	keysym quoteleft = Escape Escape
	keycode 201 = quoteleft asciitilde

(You can use xev to check to see if the does indeed generate 201 as a keycode.
Remember to click in the xev window to have it interpret keyboard events.)

You then need a file called ~/.X11Startup which contains the following line:

	xmodmap .xmodmaprc

Bill Thompson


