I had one minor problem during the compile -- using cc under OSF/1 V2.0.
In callproc.c, I got a few complaints about setpgrp using the
wrong number of arguments.  I added some #ifdef __alpha's and
got around that problem to substitute setpgid to setpgrp.
I'll put the diffs for that at the end of this message.

I'm having trouble with rmail.  When I start up rmail, I am
getting weird error messages, in particular:
	Renaming: permission denied, /etc/fstab, /etc/fstab+
I don't seem to have this problem on the version of Lucid
emacs which I compiled under Ultrix 4.4.

Now, here are the diffs for the callproc.c changes.
****************************************************************
*** callproc.c.orig	Sat May 21 09:26:45 1994
--- callproc.c	Sat May 28 12:05:21 1994
***************
*** 415,421 ****
--- 415,425 ----
  #ifdef USG
  	setpgrp ();
  #else
+ #ifdef __alpha
+ 	setpgid (pid, pid);
+ #else
          setpgrp (pid, pid);
+ #endif /* __alpha */
  #endif /* USG */
  #ifndef MSDOS
  	child_setup (filefd, fd1, fd1, new_argv, env, 0, 
***************
*** 692,698 ****
--- 696,706 ----
    setpgrp ();			/* No arguments but equivalent in this case */
  #  endif
  #  else
+ #ifdef __alpha
+   setpgid (pid, pid);
+ #else
    setpgrp (pid, pid);
+ #endif /* __alpha */
  #  endif /* USG */
  # endif /* IRIX */
    /* setpgrp_of_tty is incorrect here; it uses input_fd.  */


