In article <2s33qm$p4c@nigel.msen.com> drew@ox.com (Drew Kramer) writes:
>Is there a specific hardware reason to not support the PMAG-AA other than its
>relative age?

It's a monochrome frame buffer that arranges each bit to look like
a byte. That was a reasonable tradeoff on the MIPS which had highly
tuned code for byte-deep (dumb color) frame buffers. Alpha's don't
even have byte access, hence the do abysmal with dumb color frame
buffers (hence none is offered on them).

Believe me, you wouldn't want to run that card with an Alpha.

