Joseph Gurman writes:
>...
>    I'd like to run dvips under OSF/1 2.0 to print to an HP 4SiMX (600
>dpi). The sources at ftp.shsu.edu, aside from using default compiler
>switches for the NeXt, treat 600 dpi as imagen, 300 dpi, mag = 2. I don't
>know if this is optimal or not. So I need at least: (i) OSF/1 compilable
>sources and (ii) advice about the right MODE.
>...

I have recently installed web2c-6.1/web-6.1 and dvipsk-5.55a
on my Alpha (osf1/v1.2).
Everything works nicely, 600 dpi fonts, bigger TeX, modes...
The web2c-6.1/web2c/INSTALL file suggests getting lib-6.4.tar.gz
from ftp.cs.umb.edu:pub/tex, and you will also find the modes-1.3.mf
there as well.  This most recent version of modes.mf has
descriptions for the ljfour.  Dvipsk-5.55a also has a config.ps
file for the ljfour as the default definition for dvips output.

It is critically important to edit the kpathsea/paths.h.in file to set up
your TeX/mf heirarchy properly.  It should be the same in both
web2c and dvipsk, and it should probably conform to the lib-6.4
conventions (/usr/local/lib/texmf...).  If you have any problems,
they will probably be in your executables not finding formats,
fonts, bases, etc., or during your build the inimf or initex may
not find the modes.mf file.

I used gcc -O2 throughout.  There was only one warning in
the kpathsea build about ABS being redefined.

