X-Newsreader: TIN [version 1.2 PL2]
Xref: bga.com comp.unix.osf.osf1:1733 comp.sys.dec:3363

I was wondering if someone could shed some light on the following situation.
I have a bunch (about 50) VR319-DA Monochrome montiors connected to DECstation
5000/XXX machines via the PMAG-AA graphics card.  This guy is a 1280x1024 one
bit frame buffer kinda card, and works well with the VR319-DA under Ultrix.
I went ahead and bought some alpha systems, and after looking at the 1.2 and
1.3a kernel determined that I had half a shot at getting the PMAG to work.
Here is the structure I'm talking about:

/sys/data/tc_option_data.c:
[...]
struct tc_option tc_option [] =
{
    /*  module          driver  intr_b4 itr_aft         adpt    */
    /*  name            name    probe   attach  type    config  */
    /*  ------          ------  ------- ------- ----    ------  */

    {   "PMTNV-AA",     "nvtc",   0,      1,    'C',    0},     /* TCNVRAM */
[...]
    {   "PMAG-AA ",     "fb",     0,      0,    'C',    0},     /* MFB */
[...]
    {   "",             ""      }       /* Null terminator in the table */
};

The PMAG-AA is clearly in the TurboChannel option table.  In addition, the
file /sys/BINARY/pmagaa.o exists.

BUT, then along came 1.3b, and now the structure looks like this:
/sys/data/tc_option_data.c:
[...]
struct tc_option tc_option [] =
{
    /*  module          driver  intr_b4 itr_aft         adpt    */
    /*  name            name    probe   attach  type    config  */
    /*  ------          ------  ------- ------- ----    ------  */

    {   "PMTNV-AA",     "nvtc",   0,      1,    'C',    0},     /* TCNVRAM */
[...]
    {   "PMAGC-AA",     "pv",     0,      1,    'C',    0},     /* Low PV */
    {   "PMAGC-BA",     "pv",     0,      1,    'C',    0},     /* Mid PV */
#ifdef mips
    {   "PMAG-BA ",     "fb",     0,      0,    'C',    0},     /* CFB */
    {   "PMAG-AA ",     "fb",     0,      0,    'C',    0},     /* MFB */
[...]
#endif /* mips */
    {   "",             ""      }       /* Null terminator in the table */
};

Arg!! The device has been relegated to MIPS land!  The .o file still exists,
and a bunch of other structures are still lying about in other files.  Hmmm..

The plot thickens under 2.0.  Here the file looks like the 1.3b one, but the
pmagaa.o file is nowhere to be found.

If you have made it this far, you either have nothing better to do than read
news all day, or you really care, so here are my questions.

Is there a specific hardware reason to not support the PMAG-AA other than its
relative age?

If there is no hardware incompatability, what would be involved in either a)
writing my own driver b) convincing DEC to re-support this card?

-drew
