In article <2ra2rm$nmk@agate.berkeley.edu>, robinson@jaffna.berkeley.edu (Howard B. Robinson) writes...
>I'm trying to produce an assembly version of my f77 code by
>compiling with the -S switch. Unfortunately it doesn't work (no .s file 
>is produced).

On OSF/1, only the system C compiler can generate assembly version
with the -S switch.  The Fortran (and Pascal and cc -migrate etc.) 
compilers use a different compiler technology that produces .o files
directly without the need of an assembler.  If you just want to
look at the generated code with f77, use -V -machine_code.
Also, check out the dis command.

