>-- 
>Gary Wu
>Software Engineer
>Platforms Group
>Viewlogic Systems, Inc.			  Phone: (508) 480-0881	
>293 Boston Post Road West		  Fax:   (508) 480-0882
>Marlborough, MA  01752			  E-mail: gwu@viewlogic.com

This is what I had to do to mount a third-party external disk drive on my Sun
workstation.  First of all, the SCSI address for the external drive has to be
increased by 8.  In other words, an external drive with SCSI address 1 will be
/dev/rz9...  

Then, since the database delivered with the Alpha only lists drives
manufactured by DEC, I had to first tell it that it was a DEC drive, and then
edit the label.  As I recall, and please forgive me if my memory is a bit
fuzzy, I did something like

	disklabel -rw rz9 rz56
	disklabel -e rz9

When I editted the label, I had to change just about everything the computer
thought it knew about the disk--the number of cylinders, the number of sectors
per cylinder, etc.--as well as the partition table (including the C partition
to reflect the true size of the disk).

I don't know if that's the best way to do it or not, but it worked and wasn't
as hard as it sounds.

Good luck,

Bill Thompson


