In article <2rgif1$7du@ulowell.uml.edu> oneill@cs.uml.edu (Brian 'Doc' O'Neill) writes:
>
>My question: Does AdvFS perform faster than UFS for local traffic? NFS?
>

AdvFS is much faster for metadata operations (creation and deletion of
files). AdvFS can be slightly slower for some normal operations, but
mostly it's a wash. AdvFS can be much faster for large files when
it's builtin striping facilities are used.

AdvFS is not so much a speed enhancement (mostly because both UFS and
AdvFS are both driving I/O at platter speeds) but a functionality
enhancement.

