Quite a long time ago we ordered a CTC-3000 fast-wide SCSI controller from 
CMD for our DEC 3000 Model 400 OSF/1 box.  There were long delays, and then 
CMD announced that they were terminating work on the OSF/1 drivers.  This 
left us with a CTC-3000 board (which had been shipped in the meantime with 
VMS drivers [#!??*]), incompatible with the OS we wanted to use it with. 

So we said 'Oh well, lets use it with the OpenVMS box instead :-)' (ignoring 
that fact that for the moment there are no drivers for the board for OpenVMS 
V6.1 either...) 

But that raises the questions: 

1) Is there a fast-wide SCSI controller for the DEC 3000 400/500 from anyone 
(DEC sells the PMAZC-AA which is fast only)?  In the Seagate catalog at least 
40% od the drives they make are fast-wide.  Its hard to imagine that there 
isn't anything out there.

2) Has anyone had any experience with the CMD CTC-3000?  We have a CMD SCSI 
controller on the VAX and have been very happy, but the 'glitch' with OSF/1 
is a bit bothersome.

