
:  have problems doing an rdump from an AXP machine running OSF1 V2.0 to a
: TLZ tape drive connected to a VAX/VMS machine. All other workstation in our
: department can use this by issuing a command similar to 
: rdump some_arguments  machine_name:mkb500 /usr

: but if I do the same from our Alpha machine, I get messages like:

: rdump:rmt_reply(): Protocol to remote tape server botched
: (code %DCL-W-IVKEYW)
: rdump: Communication error in connection to remote peer
: rdump: SIGTERM received -- Try rewriting
: ..
: ..
: rdump: The ENTIRE dump is aborted

: Has anybody experiences with rdumping to VMS connected tapes?

: Thanks a lot,

: Kay

  You need to make sure that you don't get any output from SYS$SYLOGIN or
SYS$LOGIN:LOGIN.COM of which every user code is used on the VAX. Also for
OSF/1 you need add the following to the LOGIN.COM (assuming you are using
MULTINET):

$ SH :== $MULTINET_REMOTE_MAGTAPE /etc/rmt "!"

because of how DEC OSF/1 does some things.

