be able to replace the "login:" prompt in the message catalog for the
login program with whatever text you want.  Running the following
command on DEC OSF/1 1.3:

dsb@presto> dspcat /usr/lib/nls/msg/en_US.88591/login.cat | grep login:
1 : 2 login: -h for super-user only.
1 : 3 login: -f for super-user only.
1 : 21 login: no shell: %s.
1 : 22 login: 
1 : 25 Last login: %.*s 

shows that the "login:" message is number 22 in set 1 (see dspcat(1)
for details).  Knowing that, you should be able to use the gencat(1)
utility to replace the message in that slot with random text.
Then you may need to make sure the LANG or LC_MESSAGES environment
variables are set to the english locale when login is run.  No guarantees
because I didn't try it.
--
