In article 95A@cee.hw.ac.uk, iain@cee.hw.ac.uk (Iain McCrone) writes:
>Has anyone had any problems using `talk` on the DEC Alpha OSF1 boxes??
>In particular we don't seem to be able to `talk` to different architectures
>that we have within the Dept. (SUN4's and HP's).  I can `talk` DEC to DEC ok
>however, where DEC is either Ultrix boxes (5000/240) or OSF1 boxes.
>Looked at the manual page for talk and it mentioned that there might be 
>problems in some cases, is this one of them?
>
Don't know about HP, but Sun's talk is broken-- it fails to convert its data
to network byte order before sending it out.  Thus it can only talk to other
machines of the same endianness as itself, which the HPs may be (don't know).
The DEC behavior is actually correct.  Best fix: get ntalk off the Net. Archie
should be able to find it for you.  This is also discussed in the FAQ for
comp.sys.sun.admin, I believe, if you want more info.

