_arkle_2% f77 test.r
fort: Warning: test.f, line 1: Invalid statement label ignored
fort: Severe: Cannot exec process: /usr/bin/ratfor
^
fort: Severe: test.f, line 1: Missing operator or delimiter symbol
fort: Severe: Cannot exec process: /usr/bin/ratfor
------------^
fort: Warning: test.f, line 1: Missing END statement, END is assumed
fort: Severe: Cannot exec process: /usr/bin/ratfor
-------------------------------------------------^
_arkle_3% 

So the f77 compiler is out there looking for ratfor. IT IS NOT JUST
A MATTER OF DOCUMENTATION !!

I went out on the net and actually found , using archie, 
a distribution copy of ratfor.  I compiled it up using the
-taso switch, stuck it in /usr/bin and then tried it. 
