This is not a bug.  It is due to having (somehow) used up all files
handles.  When this happens any command you type has unpredictable
effects.  You should increase MAXUSERS in your kernel.  You may also
want to find out what program is causing this.  

}   Personally, my choice would be to let osf1 2.0 still hang out a bit in
}   the wonderful New England sun, and come back to it in the fall when the
}   fruit ripens and he foliage is colourful.

I disagree.  OSF2.0 is substantially better than 1.3 in its usage of
memory, kernel size, efficiency and all round bug fixes.  Unless there
is a particular extra software package (DEC or 3rd party) that is not
supported yet under 2.0, I would recommend upgrading as soon as
possible.


