option to the compilation command.  Apparently, a default executable
uses the dynamically linked libraries whereas in my situation, I need to
have the library routines "built into" the executable.  Anyway, the
"-non_shared" option fixed it and I am able to run the executable on the
Alpha that doesn't have a FORTRAN compiler.

