>"disklabel:ioctl DECWDINFO: Open partition would move or shrink.
>Use alternate partition"

I don't believe OSF will let you change the size of an open
partition.  Since you've opened the A partition, it won't
let you change the size of it.  To change the size of A
you have to use an alternate partition name, C for example.

> 
>NONE of the drive's partitions are mounted. And, I do not get this
>disklabel error when I make the "a:" partition, say, the entire disk.

