 I ran into this the other day mostly by accident, and I don't ever want to
do it again, but that's a long story. :)

 I believe what I had to do was use the '-r' switch:

  -r    Reads or writes the label directly to or from the disk, rather than
        going through the in-memory copy of the label.

 I was in single user mode after having booted off the network, trying to
