Reinhard,

yep, I agree its a problem (there was little problem with 1.1). We have 1.2
on our alphas (I assume that's what you have). bcopy and friends certainly
complained in my build tonight (only warnings tho'). Here's what I did...

 ./configure alpha-dec-osf
 [edit and comment out the `extern void' definition of `sbrk' in config.h]
 [edit fix-header.c and alter the def of `str' in the function `strdup'
  to be `const char' rather than `char']
 make LANGUAGES=c
 make stage1
 make CC="stage1/xgcc -Bstage1/" CFLAGS="-g -O"
 make stage2
 make CC="stage2/xgcc -Bstage2/" CFLAGS="-g -O"
 make compare
 make install CC="stage2/xgcc -Bstage2/" CFLAGS="-g -O" LANGUAGES=c

I still have the directory tree from which you could do the `make install'
if you like. I will contact the Stallman empire about this problem.

