>Hi ALPHA and OSF/1 wizards,
>
>I have an ALPH/AXP 3000 with an optional TURBOchanel dual scsi
>module
>that connect external 4 RZ28 disks and a cd-rom.  I have difficulty
>
>configuring the disks.  at the console prompt I did:
>>> t tc1 cnfg ,  and I get this:
>HOSTID 7
>rz000B        B/0/0
>rz100B        B/1/0
>rz200B        B/2/0
>rz300B        B/3/0
>rz500B        B/5/0
>
>and when I issued  >>show config
>the last line was like this
>
>1-PMAZB-AA    TC1      but there was not OK under DEVSTAT
>
>then when I tried to do MAKEDEV  /dev/rz000B, the systems came with
>a message
>that there is no "such device"
>
>Is there another a step I have to do before doing the MAKEDEV?
>Please help

  Have you rebuild a kernel to take this dual-SCSI module into account ?

For example, we have a 3000/500 with 2 external SCSI buses, and we were
to add the following lines in the /sys/conf/<machine> file :

bus		tcds1	at tc0 slot 1	vector tcdsintr
controller      asc2       at tcds0       slot 0 vector    ascintr
device disk		rz16	at asc2		drive 128
device disk		rz17	at asc2		drive 136
device disk		rz18	at asc2		drive 144
device disk		rz19	at asc2		drive 152
device disk		rz20	at asc2		drive 160
device disk		rz21	at asc2		drive 168
device disk		rz22	at asc2		drive 176
device disk		rz23	at asc2		drive 184 

  Moreover, I think you should use 'MAKEDEV rz16' (for example) instead of
specifying a device file, because MAKEDEV will create all the devices related
to the peripheral you specified automatically.

  Hope this helps...

