In article <MELLAN.94Apr28160452@syst06.acri.fr>, mellan@syst06.acri.fr (Alain Mellan) writes:

|> I'm running DEC OSF/1 1.2 on a couple of AXP workstations. I can't get
|> the sendmail to deliver to a local user which has a
|> "| /pipe/to/some/program" in his .forward

|> <<< 554 <"|/usr/local/bin/deliver mellan">... Cannot mail directly to programs

There is a "sendmail" security hole based on sending mail to a program.  You setup
a program in your .forward which creates a setuid shell.  Then you send yourself
mail.  If sendmail runs the program as root (or daemon) then it creats a setuid
shell owned by root or daemon.  Then you can break into the system.

It looks like your sendmail is agressively closing that hole.  There may be
a problem with the user name.  Your sendmail should be able to fork a process
that is that user to run the pipe.  I am not familiar with DEC OSF/1's sendmail,
so I cannot comment on that implementation.

