--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
			     sxperl V1.0
				  by
			  Frederic Chauveau
			    fmc@pasteur.fr


		   Dedicated to Randal L. Schwartz
                   -------------------------------

- Brief overview

Sxperl is perl5 with libsx on top.
It provides simple bindings for common Athena Widgets as perl functions.
It's certainly full of bugs...
A simple sxperl program would be :

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

package Sx;
bootstrap Sx;

sub byebye {
  local($w,$args) = @_;

  print "Bye bye (called from widget $w, arg $args)\n";
  exit;
}

&OpenDisplay('Sample sxperl');

$widget = &MakeButton('Quit', 'byebye', @ARGV[0]);

&ShowDisplay;

&MainLoop;

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All but 3 of the functions in libsx have been 'translated' to perl,
missing functions are AddReadCallback, AddWriteCallback and AddTimeOut.

- Installation

You'll need perl5alpha8 and libsx1.0

Edit the Makefile and change the various values there.
- perlsrc should be the directory containing perl.o from the perl5 distribution
- the 'libs' assume that you've installed both libperl.a and libsx.a in some
  standard place.

type make :)


you'll find 2 small sample programms quitb.pl and demo.pl you can try 
sxperl with. demo.pl is a 'translation' to perl of the demo program 
found in the libsx distribution.



