|>
|>				Fernando Gallardo
|>				e-mail: fgc@ing.puc.cl
|>

These are the kernel objects which are shipped in object form in the DEC OSF/1
kit.  You need these only if you intend to build kernels.  If you don't intend
to build kernels, you can delete the subsets that contain the objects.  Use
setld -i and find the subsets with "Kernel Objects" in their descriptions.  Then
you can use setld -d to delete those subsets.

Should you find you need to build kernels down the road, you'll need to reload
these subsets.

I'd recommend against simply deleting the .o files as this will confuse setld
should you need to load them again in the future.

Dave


