In article 3243@solaris.rz.tu-clausthal.de, buttch@trillian.in.tu-clausthal.de (Axel Buttchereit) writes:
>
>We have a pool of 5 DEC3000 running OSF/1.3a and on all machines
>we have the same problem.
>After after running some jobs that use much vm the machines `think'
>that they are nearly out of swap space:
>
>  swap space below 10%
>
>But that's not true, because all the jobs have terminated.
>
>Is there any other solution then rebooting the machines to
>`reset' the vm.
>
>
>Thanks in advance,
>
>  Axel

  Delete or rename the /sbin/swapdefault file.  When it is present
the memory needed by a program is allocated once the program is started,
even if half of this memory will actually be used.

  Deleting this file (and rebooting afterward) will cause OSF/1 to
allocate memory only when the program requires it, thus saving much of
the VM.

