We have been having an ongoing problem on our Alpha 4000/710 running OSF/1 1.3.

The symptom is that running "dump" on an active partition locks the whole
disk subsystem. This is a non-optimal failure mode, to say the least. We
originally thought the problem was due to either running OSF/1 1.3 (our
other Alpha, a 4000/610, is running OSF/1 2.0 and backs up no problem) or
because the /usr file system was over 2 GB. We reinstalled rz8 from scratch,
with OSF/1 2.0 and splitting /usr into three partitions 1GB each. Last night
I kicked off AMANDA.

*thump*

I'm running AMANDA in slave mode, so the only programs related to dump going
at the time of the hang are "dump" and "sendsize" (yes, it happens even when
it's just getting estimates!). Sometimes it does the sendsize, and dumps a
few partitions, then hangs when it gets to the partition that's active (in
fact I backed up an inactive partition on an active system with no problem).
That tends to imply it's not sendsize or senddump itself that's causing the
problem.

Any ideas?
